  "problem": "The Sources page v1.1.0 national-readiness table could present a historical Pennsylvania published-record count as current coverage. Publication manifests could close with missing assets, source-context mismatches or undeclared partial fragments. One bad dictionary asset could blank the catalog. Failed publication could replace last-good generation. Mixed catalog/dictionary generations could be served together. Sealed search lifecycle could be edited and break the search package seal.",
  "resulting_behavior": "assembleAcceptedPublicationManifest closes only when required assets, checksums and source context are present. archiveHistoricalReadiness treats corpus v1.1.0 as a historical view; Pennsylvania's 24 published records are archived and current_published_state_record_count is 0. SourcesPage labels that historical overlay as not current coverage. pageDictionary/measureAssetPage page large dictionaries predictably. serveBoundedAssets keeps the catalog available when one asset fails. Mixed generations fail closed. Failed publication leaves last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 live. Static fallback remains available. Sealed packages/search/publication-lifecycle-v2.mjs is unchanged (26572 bytes). packages/registry/index.mjs is unchanged; consumers import publication-parity.mjs directly.",
